-- title:
--   Prime-ℓ Hecke sub-ideals versus dual-pair ℓ-isogeny kernels
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of prime characteristic $q'$ which is algebraic over $\mathbb{F}_{q'}$, and let $X_0/\kappa$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve all of whose $q'$-torsion points vanish. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, that $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ becomes a division algebra over the $v$-adic completion exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda\subseteq\mathbb{H}$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication, finitely generated and $\mathbb{Q}$-spanning, maximal among such, and let $\theta$ be an injective ring homomorphism from the subring of $\operatorname{End}(X_0(\kappa))$ generated by the rationally represented homomorphisms onto $\Lambda$. Fix units $x,y$ of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{f}}$, elliptic curves $W,W'/\kappa$, nonzero rational homomorphisms $\chi\colon X_0\to W$, $\chi'\colon X_0\to W'$ and $d,d'\in\mathbb{H}^{\times}$ such that $\theta(\operatorname{Hom}(W,X_0)\circ\chi)$ is the conjugate (image under `star`) of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap x\widehat{\Lambda})$ and $\theta(\operatorname{Hom}(W',X_0)\circ\chi')$ that of $d'\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap y\widehat{\Lambda})$, where $\mathbb{H}\cap g\widehat{\Lambda}$ denotes [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19). Let $\ell\neq q'$ be a prime. Then the number of $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules $J$ of $\mathbb{H}$ of the form $\mathbb{H}\cap xh\widehat{\Lambda}$ with $h$ in the prime Hecke set $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}\ \Lambda\ \ell$ (units $h$ lying in the integral adelic box of $\Lambda$ with $\ell h^{-1}$ in that box but $h^{-1}$ and $\ell^{-1}h$ not) and satisfying $J=e\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap y\widehat{\Lambda})$ for some $e\in\mathbb{H}^{\times}$ equals the number of subgroups $C\le W(\kappa)$ with $\#C=\ell$ for which there exist rational homomorphisms $\psi\colon W\to W'$ and $\psi'\colon W'\to W$ with $\ker\psi=C$ and $\psi'\circ\psi=\ell$, $\psi\circ\psi'=\ell$.
--
--   This is the quaternion-to-curve half of Eichler's description of Brandt matrix entries at level one, in the form: sub-ideals of index $\ell^2$ of the right ideal attached to $x$ that lie in the class of the ideal attached to $y$ correspond to order-$\ell$ kernels of $\ell$-isogenies $W\to W'$ between the curves attached to $x$ and $y$ by the Deuring correspondence. It feeds the construction of the bijection between the quaternionic class set and the supersingular points used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_classSet_equiv_ssPlaces_one_kernelIdealSet_of_rationalEndSubring`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_classSet_equiv_ssPlaces_one_kernelIdealSet_of_rationalEndSubring).
